Subject: [PATCH] WowBox64: the interpreter reads FS's base from the emulator

The interpreter took FS's base from GetSegmentBase, which WowBox64 does not have, so a block
it ran read the 32-bit TEB from address 0. WowBox64 keeps the base in segs_offs[_FS].
---
--- a/src/emu/x64emu.c
+++ b/src/emu/x64emu.c
@@ -1686,6 +1686,10 @@
 #ifdef BOX64EC
     if (seg == _GS)
         return emu->win64_teb;
+#endif
+#if defined(BOX64EC) || defined(_WIN32)
+    // WowBox64 sets the 32-bit TEB as FS's base when it enters the emulation; there is no
+    // descriptor table to read it from.
     if (seg == _FS)
         return emu->segs_offs[_FS];
 #endif
